<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<SharingRules xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
      THIS COMMENT IS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT ON PURPOSE - a comment above the root breaks sf
      at source conversion.

      READ, NEVER EDIT. This object is a read-only Yardi mirror. The pattern being copied is
      Work_Order__c (excluded from DPEG_PropertyMgmt_Edit, "Yardi read-only mirror"), NOT
      sharingRules/Delinquency__c, whose Delinquency_PM_All_RW rule grants Edit to the entire
      PM group and inverts the design this build exists to implement.

      Rows are owned by whichever principal the nightly job runs as, and the object's OWD is
      Private - so WITHOUT these rules no property manager can see any receivable at all.

      🔴 DEPLOY THESE ONE AT A TIME. On this project a SharingRules payload carrying more than
      one rule fails on sharing recalculation. Deploy the file with the first rule, wait for
      recalculation to finish, then add the second and deploy again. A check-only dry run CANNOT catch
      this: check-only never performs the recalculation, so a green validation is not evidence
      that a two-rule deploy will succeed.

      CRITERIA CHOICE. Record Type would be the natural criterion for the Case rule, but for
      this object the criterion has to be a real, non-formula field: Aging_Bucket__c and
      Months_Outstanding__c are FORMULAS and criteria-based sharing cannot reference them.
      Yardi_AR_Id__c is stamped on every row the sync writes and is therefore equivalent to
      "every synced row", while still excluding hand-created junk.
    -->
    <sharingCriteriaRules>
        <fullName>Receivables_Summary_PM_Read</fullName>
        <accessLevel>Read</accessLevel>
        <description>Gives the Property Management team read access to every synced receivable. Read and never Edit - the mirror is overwritten nightly, so an edit is silently discarded on the next run, which is worse than being refused.</description>
        <label>Receivables Summary PM Read</label>
        <criteriaItems>
            <field>Yardi_AR_Id__c</field>
            <operation>notEqual</operation>
            <value></value>
        </criteriaItems>
        <sharedTo>
            <group>DPEG_Property_Mgmt_Team</group>
        </sharedTo>
    </sharingCriteriaRules>
    <sharingCriteriaRules>
        <fullName>Receivables_Summary_Principals_Read</fullName>
        <accessLevel>Read</accessLevel>
        <description>Gives the principals read access to every synced receivable, so the FSD 5.9.9 dollar-exposure ranking and the 60/90-day escalations resolve to records they can actually open. Read only - principals decide on write-offs against the Case, never against the mirror.</description>
        <label>Receivables Summary Principals Read</label>
        <criteriaItems>
            <field>Yardi_AR_Id__c</field>
            <operation>notEqual</operation>
            <value></value>
        </criteriaItems>
        <sharedTo>
            <group>Principals</group>
        </sharedTo>
    </sharingCriteriaRules>
</SharingRules>
